      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`test_kda_kernels.py` is registered for AMD CI, but `TestKDAVerifyDecodeParity` only checks `torch.cuda.is_available()`. That check is also true on ROCm, so AMD runs enter `match_cutedsl_decode`, which uses NVIDIA `ex2.approx.ftz.f32` / `lg2.approx.ftz.f32` inline assembly.\n\nThe public `fused_sigmoid_gating_delta_rule_update` entry point also lacks a platform check for this option.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Skip only `TestKDAVerifyDecodeParity` on HIP. Keep the other KDA tests enabled in AMD CI.\n- Reject `match_cutedsl_decode=True` on HIP with a clear `ValueError`, before tensor access or kernel compilation.\n- Add a platform-guard regression test that can run without a GPU.\n\n## Tests\n\nCPU execution on Linux with Python 3.12 and PyTorch 2.11.0+cu128 (GPUs hidden).\n\n```bash\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=999 SGLANG_RUST_BUILD_MODE=never SGLANG_BUILD_RUST_EXTS=none \\\n  PYTHONPATH=python python -m pytest -q \\\n  test/registered/attention/test_kda_kernels.py::TestKDADecodeParityPlatformGuard\n```\n\n**1 passed.** The same test fails against the unmodified entry point from `f7ad4345b8` because it accesses the tensors instead of rejecting HIP.\n\nAlso evaluated the test class decorators with CUDA availability true: HIP skips only the decode-parity class; NVIDIA skips none of the classes. No ROCm GPU compilation run was performed.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nThe supported kernel paths are unchanged. No numerical accuracy run was performed.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable; this adds a guard for an unsupported option and adjusts test selection.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Formatting and import order checked with Ruff and isort; `git diff --check` passed.\n- [x] Added and ran the public-entry regression test.\n- [x] Registered-test lint passed.\n- [x] No documentation update needed; no new flags or APIs.\n- [ ] ROCm hardware validation.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38718782335](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38718782335)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38718782118](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38718782118)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38718782148](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38718782148)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
